  "description": "Reid Bikes MTB Pro 27.5\" Hydro Disc| Mountain bike\nBuilt for trail riding and everyday adventures, the Reid Bikes MTB Pro 27.5\" Hydro Disc combines a lightweight alloy frame, 27.5\" wheels, front suspension and reliable hydraulic braking performance.\nThe Reid Bikes MTB Pro 27.5\" Hydro Disc is designed for riders looking for a versatile mountain bike for exploring trails, tackling uneven terrain and enjoying everyday cycling. Featuring a custom 6061 alloy frame with internal cable routing and 27.5\" wheels, it offers a stable, comfortable riding experience across a range of surfaces.\nAn 80mm suspension fork with lockout helps absorb bumps and uneven terrain, providing added comfort and control when riding off-road. The lockout function allows you to adjust the suspension for smoother surfaces, while 700mm alloy riser handlebars and comfortable Reid MTB grips offer a confident steering position.\nThe 2.35\" all-terrain MTB tyres provide reliable grip and stability across trails, gravel paths and mixed surfaces. A Shimano 3x7-speed drivetrain, featuring a 42/34/24T chainset and 14–28T freewheel, provides 21 gearing options to help tackle climbs and enjoy flatter sections of trail.\nTektro HD-M275 hydraulic disc brakes with 160mm rotors deliver reliable, controlled stopping power in changing riding conditions. A sealed bottom bracket, semi-integrated headset and double-wall alloy rims complete a durable setup designed for regular riding.\nWhether you're exploring local trails, navigating uneven urban roads or enjoying weekend rides, the Reid Bikes MTB Pro 27.5\" Hydro Disc offers a versatile combination of comfort, control and dependable mountain bike performance.\nThe Reid Bikes MTB Pro 27.5\" Hydro Disc is ideal for:\n\nTrail riding and off-road adventures, with 80mm front suspension to help absorb bumps and uneven terrain\n\nRiders looking for a versatile mountain bike, with a lightweight 6061 alloy frame and 27.5\" wheels\n\nRiding across mixed surfaces, with 2.35\" all-terrain MTB tyres for reliable grip and stability\n\nComfortable, confident handling, with 700mm alloy riser handlebars and Reid MTB grips\n\nTackling climbs and descents, with a Shimano 21-speed drivetrain offering a choice of gearing options\n\nReliable stopping power, with Tektro hydraulic disc brakes and 160mm rotors\n\nAdapting to different riding conditions, with a suspension fork featuring a lockout function\n\nWeekend adventures and everyday cycling, with a versatile setup suited to trails, paths and recreational riding",
